    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration date's year.\n\nSince this is a purely derived, response-only value (as the test's comment notes, \"Derived from the owner's own fields, so seed-independent\"), I followed the codebase's existing pattern for computed owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than storing it:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient public String getMembershipNumber()` that composes `customerCode` and `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`, returning null if either source field is absent (avoids NPEs when mapping seed/legacy owners).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct's `toOwnerDto` maps it automatically into every owner response (POST create and GET).\n\nThe target `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
